## SCREENING FOR CHRONIC COMPLICATIONS

- GLYPH&lt;127&gt; Measure blood pressure at every scheduled visit, review medication as per hypertension protocol
- GLYPH&lt;127&gt; REFER for dilated-pupil retinal exam upon diagnosis, and every two years thereafter, or as per ophthalmologist recommendation
- GLYPH&lt;127&gt; Examine feet for ulcers at every visit. REFER to higher level of care if ulcer present
- GLYPH&lt;127&gt; Assess risk of lower limb amputation annually (foot pulses, sensory neuropathy by monofilament, presence of healed or open ulcers, calluses). REFER to higher level of care if ulcer present or pulse absent
- GLYPH&lt;127&gt; Test for proteinuria annually. REFER to higher level of care if positive.

## MANAGEMENT OF ACUTE COMPLICATIONS

Severe hypoglycaemia (plasma glucose &lt;50 mg/dl or 2.8 mmol/l) or signs:

- GLYPH&lt;127&gt; If conscious, give a sugar-sweetened drink
- GLYPH&lt;127&gt; If unconscious, give 20-50 mI of 50% glucose (dextrose) IV over 1-3 minutes.

Severe hyperglycaemia

(plasma glucose &gt;18 mmol/l (325 mg/dl) and urine ketone 2+) or signs and symptoms of severe hyperglycaemia:

- GLYPH&lt;127&gt; Set up intravenous drip 0.9% NaCI 1 litre in 2 hours; continue at 1 litre every 4 hours, REFER to hospital.
